>>>>> "Jimmy" == Jimmy Eng <engj@u.washington.edu> writes:
In article <3vb6bn$245@nntp5.u.washington.edu> engj@u.washington.edu (Jimmy Eng) writes:


Jimmy> I'm trying to place an external Maxtor 1.2GB hard drive onto
Jimmy> a newly acquired DEC3000-300 running but I'm starting to
Jimmy> believe that I have a bad drive.

Jimmy> The drive is set to scsi id 4.  Here are some of the problems
Jimmy> I run into:

>> disklabel -rw rz4 MXT-1240S
Jimmy> disklabel: ioctl DIOCWDINFO: I/O error

Instead of the above command, just use 

	disklabel -rw rz4 rz4

which forces disklabel to send the properl enquiry commands to the
disk to read the geometry it has.  Then to newfs the disk do:

	newfs -n -v /dev/rrz4c /dev/rrz4c

Though I really prefer to use advfs since it's more flexible and much
much faster rebooting after a power outage, crash, etc.

John



