It depends which version of perl5 you are trying to compile.  The
latest official version is 5.001, and there is a set of official
unoffical patches that brings it to perl5.001m.  You can find this on
ftp.wpi.edu:/perl5/perl5.001m.tar.gz

Once you have gotten the file and untarred it, all you should have to
do to configure perl for installation in /usr/local/... is:

	./Configure -des
	make
	make test
	make install

This will use the default answers to setup perl5.  Let me know if you
have any problems.





