Hello folks!

	I'm keen to purchase an Alpha low-end workstation for use at home, and
my original thought was that I'd set this up on an ISDN line to communicate
with
the office via some intermediate service provider such as NetCom. Where I live
(SF Bay Area), ISDN is just becoming available for home phones.

	I already have a 3000-300LX, which has an ISDN adapter on it. Naturally,
I assumed that the newer ws's would have an ISDN port too. Surprisingly, this
is
not the case. A call in to technical support at 1-800-Digital reveal a further
puzzle - the ISDN port on the TurboChannel alpha was never supported by any
Digital-supplied hardware neither VMS or OSF. It appears that DEC is not going
to support ISDN.

	Does anyone have any further info on ISDN and Alpha systems? Have I been
given the correct information? (my local dec rep has never heard of ISDN). Does
anyone have any suggestions on how I might link a home machine with the office
system, other than ISDN?

regards
Tony Cox




