It seems that Advfs in 3.2A is quite stable. I haven't seen any of those
usual kernel panics in this version. _But_ Advfs is not suitable for 
using as a filesystem for news spool. It's a good thing to have your 
news spool in one file system. Advfs are at this time not able to handle 
that many files, and our contact in DEC could not give any date
when this would be fixed, if fixed at all.

We are using LSM with striping for our news servers, currently there
are 1.400.000 files in news spool distributed between to 4GB disks.
This setup seems to perform reasonably well, news.daily uses about
two to three hours to complete. (DEC 2100 4/100) And we have never
experienced any problems of any kind.

Ole Troan



