With the dates

aharon> gcc-osf-1.39.19.tar.gz 1799624 Jan 19 1992
aharon> gcc-osf-1.39.19.tar.gz 1799624 Jan 20 1992
aharon> gcc-osf-1.39.17.tar.Z  2625713 Feb 17 1992
aharon> gcc-osf-1.39.3.tar.Z   2540357 May 17 1991

From the dates and version numbers, I'm pretty sure these are from
Michael Meissner's MIPS branch of gcc v1.39 back when he was working
at the OSF.  These will work on a DECstation running OSF/1, or any of
several platforms with MIPS cpus (but gcc has advanced considerably
since then, so I can't see why you would want to use it).  It will not
work on Alphas (remember, osf1 isn't exclusively DEC), which you could
probably guess just from the dates.

For Alphas runing Digital Unix, you want gcc 2.6.0 or later
(preferably later)--the standard 2.7.0 distrbution builds fine for
most people, modulo some bogus ld warnings under 3.2.  Unfortunately,
I don't know of a site with binaries for DUX archived, so I don't have
an answer to the original question.
