Ratish J. Punnoose (punnoose@pluto.ee.cua.edu) wrote:

:  I am running OSF/1 3.2 on an Alpha Station.  I have trying in vain to 
: enforce file system quotas.  I can use the edquota command and the 
: vedquota (for the Advanced FileSystem).  But I do not know what to enter 
: when the editor comes up.  I could not find any documentation on the 
: format of the file to be edited.  Could someone please tell me the format 
: of the file which is edited by the edquota command?

Your problem is probably that you have not set up the file systems for
quota accounting, therefore "edquota" or "vedquota" come up with an
empty screen. Once you have edited /etc/fstab and started quota accounting
with "quotaon" or "vquotaon", the (v)edquota command comes up with a
template that is fairly self-explaining (except that you never know how
much a "block" is, usually it's 1024 bytes).

A typical entry in /etc/fstab for quotas looks like the following:

file_domain#fset /filesystem     advfs rq,userquota,groupquota 0 0
