rschuhl@rsl000.rhein-main.de (Robert Schuhl) writes:

>Try to use the old (3.0) nfsd, and the other nfs stuff in Version 3.2.

Don't!  nfsd and nfsiod simply setup a socket or so, register with portmap,
fork a few times, and dive into the kernel where the real NFS code is.
In V3.2 the NFS server sets up kernel threads and nfsd no longer has to
fork.  Running the V3.0 nfsd on V3.2 will not work.
