Our alpha's running OSF1 v3.0 occasionally accumulate large numbers of defunct
processes, and even though a 'ps -l' shows init to be their parent process,
init does not seem to reap them.  Has anyone else observed this behaviour?  Is
there a fix to make these processes go away?

One system has been up for 3 days and has 50 defunct processes out of a total
of 297.  Since the parent process is pid 1, it's hard to figure out where
they are coming from.

I think these defunct processes are supposed to have released all their memory,
but the system's swap is >90% full, and looking at the output from ps, I can't
see what is using it all.  Is it possible that they are still holding onto VM,
even though ps says they aren't?

Thanks for any advice...

Duncan



