You could /etc/passwd on the NIS master the "master" file for the passwd
maps.  Then you can use passwd to change passwords, followed by remaking
the maps.  This solution does prevent you from restricting access to the
NIS master though. 

If the above solution is not acceptable, your other choice would be to
write a perl or C program to muck with the file you're building the maps
from. The perl book has a passwd program in it, and the source is available
from

  ftp://ftp.ora.com/pub/examples/nutshell/programming_perl/perl.tar.Z 

Note that this passwd program won't let you use dictionary words, two word
combinations, etc as passwords.


