cannell@pt9531.ped.pto.ford.com (Larry Cannell) wrote:
>Tony Arnold (tony.arnold@mcc.ac.uk) wrote:
>: Has anyone had success in connecting Exceed 4.1 on a PC to a Digital 
>: Alpha 3.2 system using xdmcp? When we try it we get authenticatin error, 
>: but cannot find what authentication or how to fix it.
>
>Version 4.x of Exceed will insist on using XDM-AUTHENTICATION if you put
>something in the "key" field under Xconfig/Communications. This type of
>authentication requires predefined keys on both ends (and is just basically
>a pain in the tush if you don't need it). After upgrading to OSF/1 3.0 xdm
>started using XDM-AUTHENTICATION as its default authentication. 
>
>You could change the "key" field or switch back to the 2.x version of xdm.

Thanks Larry for this advice, it gave us the info we needed to get things 
going.

To summarise, we set the 'key' field in Exceeds configuration to be blank 
and in the security section enabled remote hosts to modify the access 
control list.

It all worked beautifully after this.

