In article <3ug969$9pk@nrcnet0.nrc.ca> johnston@nrc.ca (Daniel F. Johnston (Dan)) writes:

Daniel> Is there a turbochannel network interface for the Alpha 3000
Daniel> series of computer that will support 100BaseT ethernet?  (This
Daniel> is on DEC UNIX (currently 3.2)).  If so does anyone know how
Daniel> well this works?  Can I use both interfaces (ie the existing
Daniel> 10 meg) and thus put only selected traffic over the fast line?

The TurboChannel bus is a dead end these days, with DEC moving all the
new systems to PCI, so don't expect to see any more cards unless a
third party manufacturer thinks they can make money with it.  So in
general, you won't be able to get a 100BaseT interface for your
system. 

Digital Unix does support multiple network interfaces in a single
system, and you can route traffic over an interface using various
criteria, but I haven't done much with this here.

