On Digital UNIX (nee DEC OSF/1) version up to V4.0 (entering field test
soon), there is a 1-to-1 one correspondence of user threads to kernel
threads, based on the original Mach threading model. The threads package
is called DECthreads, and corresponds to draft 4 of pthread (POSIX P1003.1c,
nee .4a).

On version V4.0, we'll be moving to a mixed threading model, combining
kernel-based and library-based threads in a many-to-one model. This
release will be based on the final, approved pthreads standard of June 1995.
