In article <victor-1207950949590001@190.10.20.51>, victor@ctechnics.oz.au (Victor Yu) writes:
|> Does OSF/1 support multithreading(MT) and other MT related functions such
|> as code segment locking and semphore. I'm from Solaris background and have
|> not seem OSF/1 before. Is it system V compliant? Any help are appreciated.
|> 
|> Victor.
|> 

	Yes, Digital UNIX (former DEC OSF/1) supports Kernel threads based
	on POSIX p-threads. Threads have full parellel processing capabilities
	in multirpocessor systems. P-threads support all you ask.

	Standard Digital UNIX is compatible with BSD and System V, and if 
	you wish full System V R4 compatibility, you can always install
	so called System V Subset from Complementary Products CS.

	Best regards,

