Yes, Digital UNIX (aka DEC OSF/1) supports multithreading, semaphores,
memory locking, etc., through our POSIX threads and realtime libraries
(libpthreads and librt). See the Guild to DECthreads and the Guide
to Realtime Programming in the online or hardcopy documentation for
more details.
