I'm trying to get NIS and Enhanced Security to work together on a
DEC3000 running dUnix 3.2.  In theory, it looks like everything is in
place, but when I try to change my password, it says it "couldn't
change passwd".  The doc implies that it doesn't like my password, but
it should be fine.  It looks more like it couldn't find or access the
correct file.  (rpc.yppasswdd is running).

My understand is that with NIS and Enhanced Security in place, the
passwords are actually maintained in /var/yp/prpasswd rather than
/etc/passwd or /tcb/files/auth/*.  As I said, everything looks right
to me and I have got it so that it accepts the password I started
with.  I'd like to get the server running correctly before I even
think about the client systems.

Along the same lines, it appears that yppasswd requires the original
password, even when root is changing a user's password.  Is there a
work around for this?  I'm constantly changing passwords for people
who've forget theirs and manually blanking out the password field in
prpasswd is going to be annoying.

