Hi all,
	We just got a DEC Alpha 3000/900 running OSF v3.0, and there are some
annoyances we haven't been able to puzzle out yet from the docs, man pages, and
FAQ.  Here goes :

1) passwd forces one to not use an all lowercase password.  Seems like we
   should be able to choose anything, if we really really want to - how can we
   override this safety feature?

2) telnet seems to be defaulting to telnet -l.  That is, it automatically
   sends off your current username when you telnet somewhere.  Very annoying -
   how to turn this off?

3) how do we authorize accounts to be able to su to root?  As shipped, the only
   way to go root was to login on console, and allowing telnet to root via
   /etc/secttys makes me cringe.

Thanks in advance,

