CHORUS/Fusion supports multi-threaded UNIX processes (user and kernel
level threads, i.e. one thread doing e.g. a blocking read(2) on a tty
will not block other threads in the same process). The multi-thread
API is POSIX 1003.1c (former .4a) compatible. CHORUS/Fusion is binary
compatible with SCO Open Desktop 3.0. For more information on CHORUS/Fusion,
see URL ftp://ftp.chorus.fr/pub/datasheets/Fusion_r1.ascii).

