Jari Tavi <jpt@rixrax.fno.dec.com> wrote:
>	If you really mean what you say, then your comment contains 
>	conflicting statements:
>
>		light weight processes != kernel threads

They're only unequal if you choose not to use the phrase "lightweight
processes" to refer to kernel threads.

Sun, for example, uses the term "lightweight process", in SunOS 5.x, to
refer to threads of control known to the the kernel; user-mode threads
are implemented atop them, but there isn't necessarily a one-to-one
correspondence between user-mode threads and LWP's.

Unixware 2.x may do the same thing, and Novell may use the term
"lightweight process" in the same way that Sun does.



