1. Use "dxkeycaps" to edit the keycaps.
   (You can find the utility in the session manager
    under "Options" - "Keyboard..." - "Edit Keycaps...")

2. Save the result in your home directory as ".dxkeycaps".

3. Add something like "xmodmap $HOME/.dxkeycaps" in your 
   ".X11Startup" file.
   (If you don't have an ".X11Startup" file, create one in
    your home directory)

Good Luck !




