zmodem through a terminal server running lat.  The zmodem package I'm using
is the Omen Technologies package.

What I'm having trouble with is moving compressed data files.  If I attempt
to send a compressed file, file.tar.gz for instance, I get CRC errors like
crazy on a download and can't get anything at all on uploads.  The strange
part is that uncompressed data seems to move fine, at least for downloading.
This problem is not restricted to tar.gz files either.  I get the same
results using .zip and .arj files.  It also doesn't seem to be an ascii/binary
thing, since tar files alone transfer fine.

