To overcome the negative effects of disk I/O why not use asynchronous reads
and writes? The aio_result_t structure whose address is passed to the read
and write functions and returned by aiowait() could be appended with infor-
mation that identified the particular thread from which the operation orig-
inated. Of course not all platforms support asynchronous I/O, but it'd be
silly to not take advantage of that if it were available. 

