You need to create a passwd file under the /etc directory of your ftp
chrooted directory.  (~/ftp/etc/passwd).  This should not be your real
password file.  All encrypted passwords in the fake passwd file should be
replaced with an *.  You only need the users that own files under the ftp
directory in this passwd file.

Sample entry:
root:*:0:1:Big Brother:/:

This file should be mode 111 (only read access to everyone).

Hope This Helps

Jason



