mikeb@ccs.neu.edu (Michael Bukhin) wrote:
>There is now a machine on our network running osf 3.xx that has a massive
>tape drive.  Without NFS, is there any simple way I can backup our
>storage machine onto the the drive of the 3.xx box?  I really don't want
>to mess with NFS.  BTW the hard drive of the tape drive box doesn't have
>the capacity to store an enormous tar, though it has a good amount of
>space and thus could store temporary smaller files.  thanks
>
>-mike
>
try the gnu tar with

tar cvf remotemachine:/dev/rmt??? your_files....

or you can try

tar cvbf 20 - your_files|rsh remotemachine dd of=/dev/rmt??? obs=20b


what you need in both cases is an account on the "remotemachine", where you can
do a rlogin without a password (.rhosts - entry)

Joerg
