<bear@fysik.ou.dk> says:
>
>dbkatz@facstaff.wisc.edu (Don Katz) wrote:
>>I'd like to get a cable to run the internal SCSI bus (DEC 
>>3000/600) outside of the system case and attach some additional 
>>drives (to use the other 3 SCSI ID's). Is this supported? Can it 
>>be done? and if so, what cable do I need and where can I get 
>>one?
>
Yes, I know its "not supported" but it sure does work.  I recently
had our '600 open.  The end of the A bus ended at the CD.  There
is only 1 internal disk on our system, so the cable was simply
"reconfigured" to go directly to the CD from the disk which left
a balance of cable that was long enough to go to the rear panel.

Vacant Turbo channel slot now has a plate with 'Centronics' type
connector and a 1 inch ribbon to male DIL connector.  Removing the
terminator, plugging into the adaptor, and voila'.

Use short, good quality SCSI cables outside, and home free.

We have so much stuff around the campus spewing RF noise, that
the FCC would have trouble finding the building, let alone
the machine :)

