Marius (booysems@telkom09.telkom.co.za) wrote:
>Hi,

>I am trying to label a rz28 disk. I have zeroed the label and when trying to 
>re-label, it complains about having an open partition that would move or 
>shrink. Is there a way that I can have a look at which partition is open? Can 
>I close it? (the disk is not being used), or am I missing something here?

>Thank you.
>Marius.

I had the same problem.  It turns out that "disklabel rz3" (for example)
will open rz3a as its default partition.  Because this opens rz3a, you
can't move or shrink the a partition.  You should be able to move or shrink
any other partition, but to move/shrink the a partition, try
"disklabel /dev/rrz3c" (or any other partition that starts at offset 0).

