Dan.Pop@mail.cern.ch (Dan Pop) writes:

>> The Station is a DEC3000/300, with 32 Mo. RAM.
>> is it a memory problem ? 
..
>> Is there any way to get this mwm faster ?

>Add more memory.  Dunno about 48 MB, but 64 MB is OK for a single user
>workstation running OSF/1.  This is the only effective way to tune the
>performance of an OSF/1 system with 32 MB of RAM.  Everything else is a
>waste of time.

I've tried 3.2 with CDE, which should be a worst case.  Unbearable on
32 MB, fine on 48 MB.  So I think 48 MB is enough.  However I find
that I'm happy on a 32 MB 3000/300LX using fvwm as the window manager,
and xemacs (the emacs that comes with OSF/1 -- based on version 18)
rather than emacs version 19 (which is slow to start even on big
machines).  So you may be able to tune by choosing software that is
smaller in memory usage.  That's fine for a while, but in the long run
you probably don't want a machine that requires you to use cut-down
versions of all the applications.

I've heard rumors that 4.0 is intended to work OK even with CDE on a
32 MB machine.  That would be a massive accomplishment in tuning,
though Sun did the equivalent in going from Solaris 2.3 to 2.4, so
it's not impossible.

I'm still going to try to swing an upgrade to 48 MB for all of our
Alphas.




