dbkatz@facstaff.wisc.edu (Don Katz) wrote:
>I'd like to get a cable to run the internal SCSI bus (DEC 
>3000/600) outside of the system case and attach some additional 
>drives (to use the other 3 SCSI ID's). Is this supported? Can it 
>be done? and if so, what cable do I need and where can I get 
>one?

Well, it is most certainly NOT supported. But yes, it is possible.
As to getting the cable, well, I'd ask somebody in your electronics
shop to make it for you. If you have a vacant TURBOchannel slot, then
you could mount another 50-pin Amphenol connector in the unused cutout.
Use an Amphenol connector that clips on to the ribbon cable - that it
the easiest way. Now, I don't have a 600 here (we have a 400), so check
if the internal scsi cable ends in a female 50 pin DIL connector (like
the ones that go on the harddisks) with an active terminator plugged in.
That is how it is done on my DECpc XL. Anyway, if that is the case then 
you simple buy a female 50 pin DIL and connect to the other end of the
ribbon cable from the Amphenol and plug that in instead of the active 
terminator. From the Amphenol to your new expansion box(es) you use 
SHORT cables, and the last box must evidently have a proper terminator 
(you can get away with leaving the terminator resistors in place on the 
last drive, but that is generally a bad idea).

I didn't say this, and I'm ceratinly not to blame if you stuff it!

Have fun.

Bear
