Daniel Anderson (andersdc@net-works.net) wrote:

: I am having a problem with Getopts running perl5 on a DEC Alpha 
: with OSF/1.  The script core dumps in the Getopts routine...

I'm not sure I have a solution, but definitely I had the same problem.
I traced it to the "eval"-statements in the Getopts routine. The perl 5
version of eval behaves rather differently from its perl 4 predecessor, but
I don't know what the differences are - except that perl 5 eval on OSF/1
sometimes dumps core.

I implemented a brute-force workaround: I modified the Getopts routine
to produce an associative array $opt_{"h"}, $opt_{"v"}, ...,  rather than
single variables $opt_h, $opt_v etc.; this can be done without an eval.
Of course, this requires analogous modifications of all programs
calling the Getopts routine.
