Which Fortran compiler (f77 or f90) and what version are you using?  Can
you post (or mail me) some sample code to look at?  Have you tried 
DECladebug on it?  DECladebug has very good (and ever getting better)
support for Fortran.  

From the symptoms, I'd say that dbx & gdb are decoding the parameters 
NELE and PHIO incorrectly.  The large hex number (actually, a small 
negative offset) generally indicate parameters passed on the stack,
rather than in registers.  I'd need to see the symbol type and storage
class information to be sure.  Are they dynamic arrays by any chance?

