desktops, supports 3d, motif-like look & feel) on all my machines.

The sizes of the binaries in question are as follows.  Note that this
may not be totally accurate because of memory that's dynamically
allocated when the programs are running:

<2:41pm>renoir/gallatin:namedfiles>size `which mwm`
text    data    bss     dec     hex
409600  81920   7680    499200  79e00
<2:41pm>renoir/gallatin:namedfiles>size `which twm`
text    data    bss     dec     hex
172032  32768   13168   217968  35370
<2:41pm>renoir/gallatin:namedfiles>size `which ctwm`
text    data    bss     dec     hex
278528  57344   9008    344880  54330

I dislike fvwm for a variety of reasons including: 
- no icon manager out-of-the-box
- was designed to be tiny, but has suffered from so much creeping
   featurism that its as large as *twm and even its author prefers ctwm!

To save memory, you may want to consider ditching dxsession and
writing a decent .xsession file for each user (or altering 
/usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xsession to use twm & xterm instead of dxsession).

Drew



